    "summary": "Liibaan Axmed Xasan, the Justice and Welfare Party (JSP) candidate for Galmudug leadership, has accepted the decision by the national electoral commission to re-run the regional elections. The move follows a Supreme Court ruling that annulled the August 2026 results.",
    "content": "Liibaan Axmed Xasan, the candidate of the Justice and Welfare Party (JSP) for the presidency of Galmudug, has publicly endorsed the decision by the Independent National Electoral and Boundaries Commission to hold a new vote in the region. The announcement comes after the Supreme Court, on August 24, 2026, invalidated the results of the simultaneous elections for the House of Representatives and local councils in Galmudug, instructing the electoral body to organize a fresh poll.\n\nIn a statement, Xasan called on the people of Galmudug to prepare for the upcoming elections, emphasizing the importance of a transparent and credible process. He reiterated his commitment to respecting the rule of law and the decisions of the country's judicial and electoral institutions. The candidate's acceptance is seen as a step toward de-escalating tensions that arose following the controversial results.\n\nThe Supreme Court's ruling and the subsequent decision by the electoral commission have been widely anticipated by political observers, who noted irregularities in the electoral process. The re-run is expected to take place in the coming weeks, with preparations already underway. This development is crucial for the stability of Galmudug, which has experienced political turbulence over the past year.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this news is significant as it reflects the ongoing efforts to establish democratic governance in Somalia. Many diaspora members have vested interests in Galmudug, both economically and politically, and look to these elections as a barometer for the country's political trajectory. Transparent elections are essential for fostering trust in the federal system and encouraging diaspora engagement in national affairs.\n\nThe JSP candidate's cooperative stance may set a precedent for other political actors in the region, signaling a willingness to prioritize institutional integrity over personal ambition. As the electoral process moves forward, all eyes will be on Galmudug to see if the re-run proceeds smoothly and peacefully.",
